faqs:
  - question: What is a healthy cholesterol level?
    answer: >-
      As a general guide, total cholesterol of 5 or below and "bad" LDL
      cholesterol of 3 or below (in mmol/L) are healthy for most adults. Your
      target may be lower if you have heart disease or diabetes. Your doctor
      will look at your overall risk, not just the numbers.
  - question: Can thin people have high cholesterol?
    answer: >-
      Yes. Genes play a big part. Around 1 in 250 people has an inherited
      condition called familial hypercholesterolaemia, which causes very high
      cholesterol from birth.
---

**Cholesterol** is a fatty substance in your blood. Your body needs some, but too much of the wrong kind can build up in your blood vessels and narrow them. This raises your risk of a **heart attack**, **stroke** and other circulation problems. More than half of adults in the UK have cholesterol above the healthy level.

## Symptoms

High cholesterol **does not cause symptoms**. The only way to know is a **blood test**.

## Good and bad cholesterol

- **LDL** (sometimes called bad cholesterol) can build up in blood vessels
- **HDL** (sometimes called good cholesterol) helps remove cholesterol
- **non-HDL** cholesterol is all the cholesterol that is not HDL. Doctors often use it to decide on treatment

## What raises cholesterol?

- eating a lot of **saturated fat**, found in fatty meat, butter, cheese, cakes and biscuits
- not being active, being overweight, smoking and drinking a lot of alcohol
- conditions such as **type 2 diabetes**, an **underactive thyroid** and **kidney disease**
- your **genes**, including **familial hypercholesterolaemia (FH)**

## Getting checked

In England, adults aged **40 to 74** without a heart or circulation condition are invited for a free **NHS Health Check** every 5 years. It includes a cholesterol test and works out your chance of a heart attack or stroke in the next 10 years, using a tool called **QRISK**. You can also ask your GP or some pharmacies for a test.

Read about [treatment for high cholesterol](/conditions/heart-and-circulation/high-cholesterol/treatment/).
